00:02:41.859 --> 00:02:44.776
And the Pope said sounds good.

00:02:44.776 --> 00:02:46.566
And so the Pope went
over the Michael Angelo

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:50.733
and said, I want you to
restore the greatness of Rome.

00:02:52.606 --> 00:02:56.360
And the greatness of Rome
is now on your shoulders

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.616
because I want you to
pain the Sistine Chapel.

00:02:59.616 --> 00:03:02.074
And I want you to make it
a masterpiece that holds

00:03:02.074 --> 00:03:04.701
the world in awe when they see it.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:07.119
And Michael Angelo replied to the Pope.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:10.617
He said, ya know, I'm not a painter.

00:03:10.617 --> 00:03:13.867
And I've never painted, I'm a sculptor.

00:03:15.123 --> 00:03:17.669
But Julius the II was very persistent

00:03:17.669 --> 00:03:19.587
and eventually Michael Angelo said fine,

00:03:19.587 --> 00:03:23.754
I'm going to agree and over
four years, four hard years,

00:03:24.922 --> 00:03:27.424
four years that took
incredible self control,

00:03:27.424 --> 00:03:30.094
incredible grit, we're going
to talk about grit in this

00:03:30.094 --> 00:03:33.566
webinar, incredible focus,
incredible discipline.

00:03:33.566 --> 00:03:37.782
Michael Angelo created the Sistine Chapel.

00:03:37.782 --> 00:03:39.743
Now let's put this into perspective.

00:03:39.743 --> 00:03:42.499
I mean, Michael Angelo had
never painted Fresco before.

00:03:42.499 --> 00:03:46.255
Michael Angelo had to paint
something on the ceiling

00:03:46.255 --> 00:03:49.055
of the Sistine Chapel that
people standing many feet

00:03:49.055 --> 00:03:52.195
below could look up at
and see with great detail.

00:03:52.195 --> 00:03:55.272
Michael Angelo dealt with
the fact that the painting

00:03:55.272 --> 00:03:57.896
