00:10:26.807 --> 00:10:29.357
- Your hardest tasks, you
should set for the morning.

00:10:29.357 --> 00:10:31.783
In the morning, you typically
have the highest will power.

00:10:31.783 --> 00:10:34.871
Your brain is refreshed,
glucose stores are pretty good

00:10:34.871 --> 00:10:36.503
even though you've been fasting overnight.

00:10:36.503 --> 00:10:38.381
You're refreshed, you're ready to go.

00:10:38.381 --> 00:10:40.094
You're more likely to make smart decisions

00:10:40.094 --> 00:10:41.886
because you can think, you have clarity.

00:10:41.886 --> 00:10:43.508
You're not exhausted by the day yet.

00:10:43.508 --> 00:10:46.306
So whatever is hard for you,
whether that's exercise,

00:10:46.306 --> 00:10:48.222
some new thing you're
trying to do, try to do it

00:10:48.222 --> 00:10:51.268
before your day, before
the long day which is why

00:10:51.268 --> 00:10:53.852
most successful people
in history have some kind

00:10:53.852 --> 00:10:56.016
of smart morning routine so they wake up,

00:10:56.016 --> 00:10:59.269
they do the most important
task first while they're fresh

00:10:59.269 --> 00:11:01.023
and then do the rest of the
stuff throughout the day

00:11:01.023 --> 00:11:03.437
or at the end of the day
when they're more tired.

00:11:03.437 --> 00:11:05.271
- [Narrator] Before you
start to seriously build

00:11:05.271 --> 00:11:08.525
your self discipline, the
first thing you're going

00:11:08.525 --> 00:11:10.031
to do is learn how to make it easier

00:11:10.031 --> 00:11:12.905
on your future self to complete a task.

00:11:12.905 --> 00:11:15.243
Think of it as stretching before a run.

00:11:15.243 --> 00:11:17.164
Take out your WellCast
Journal and write down

00:11:17.164 --> 00:11:20.130
a task that you regularly put off.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.796
Let's say there's a big pile of dishes

00:11:21.796 --> 00:11:24.176
that greets you every day after work.

00:11:24.176 --> 00:11:26.500
And instead of cleaning them right up,

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:29.162
you bow to the temptation
of collapsing on your couch

00:11:29.162 --> 00:11:31.538
and leave them until the
next morning when you tell

00:11:31.538 --> 00:11:35.087
yourself, you have time
to take care of them.

00:11:35.087 --> 00:11:38.471
So help your future
self out, write down two

00:11:38.471 --> 00:11:40.595
things that you're going
to do to make it easier

00:11:40.595 --> 00:11:43.353
for you to complete the task the next day.

00:11:43.353 --> 00:11:46.601
Stack the dishes neatly
in the sink or scrape the

00:11:46.601 --> 00:11:50.143
food off any especially dirty
plates before turning in.

00:11:50.143 --> 00:11:52.935
And that brings us to Workout Two.

00:11:52.935 --> 00:11:55.767
Now that you've started
stretching your muscles,

00:11:55.767 --> 00:11:58.144
let's try a conditioning exercise.

00:11:58.144 --> 00:12:01.482
Okay, now the same scenario
greets you when you

00:12:01.482 --> 00:12:04.486
return home from work, you're tired.

00:12:04.486 --> 00:12:07.276
It's been a long day
and the dirty mountain

00:12:07.276 --> 00:12:10.032
of dishes is sitting in your sink.

00:12:10.032 --> 00:12:11.866
This time, figure out a way to

00:12:11.866 --> 00:12:14.911
break the activity into segments.

00:12:14.911 --> 00:12:16.415
Take out your WellCast
Journal and write down

00:12:16.415 --> 00:12:18.693
a week's plan for how you're going

00:12:18.693 --> 00:12:21.235
to tackle this task gradually.

00:12:21.235 --> 00:12:24.407
For example, the first
night, do five dishes.

00:12:24.407 --> 00:12:28.299
The second night, do seven,
slowly increase how many you do.

00:12:28.299 --> 00:12:31.510
Your discipline will slowly build as well.

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:34.342
Like any exercise,
building up your will power

00:12:34.342 --> 00:12:36.692
will take time and effort but you

00:12:36.692 --> 00:12:39.275
keep at it, you'll see results.

00:12:40.192 --> 00:12:42.778
- If you want to increase
your willpower, you

00:12:42.778 --> 00:12:45.568
need to remember your
why, remember the big

00:12:45.568 --> 00:12:47.530
game that you are trying to play.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.873
And for me, this is something
that I need to do daily.

00:12:49.873 --> 00:12:53.081
I find that no matter how
great a day, it's video day.

00:12:53.081 --> 00:12:55.459
It's filming day for me,
I'm pumped, I'm excited.

00:12:55.459 --> 00:12:58.207
I leave here feeling amazed and energized.

00:12:58.207 --> 00:13:00.123
No matter how great a
day I had, the next day

00:13:00.123 --> 00:13:03.791
I start from scratch, the
next day I'm starting over.

00:13:03.791 --> 00:13:05.458
The next day I need to
build myself up again

00:13:05.458 --> 00:13:07.878
as part of my morning
routine and ritual to remind

00:13:07.878 --> 00:13:11.176
myself to push harder,
to do more, to not stop,

00:13:11.176 --> 00:13:13.968
to not rest, to not
stay in my comfort zone.

00:13:13.968 --> 00:13:16.346
It's a daily battle and
a daily grind and I think

00:13:16.346 --> 00:13:20.308
having that morning routine
becomes so so so so important

00:13:20.308 --> 00:13:21.896
to help you remember you why.

00:13:21.896 --> 00:13:23.564
I think you can only force
yourself to do something

00:13:23.564 --> 00:13:26.191
for so long before you quit.

00:13:26.191 --> 00:13:28.487
If you don't like the
work that you're doing,

00:13:28.487 --> 00:13:30.785
if you're not genuinely
excited about the work

00:13:30.785 --> 00:13:33.621
that you're going to do today,
that can only last for so long.

00:13:33.621 --> 00:13:35.791
You can only increase you
will power to do something

00:13:35.791 --> 00:13:38.713
that you don't want to do
for so long before you quit

00:13:38.713 --> 00:13:40.303
and realize, this isn't for me.

00:13:40.303 --> 00:13:41.641
I got to move on and do something else.

00:13:41.641 --> 00:13:43.774
But it's for the things
that we do want to do.

00:13:43.774 --> 00:13:46.036
It's for the big dreams
that we have that sometimes

00:13:46.036 --> 00:13:48.250
we don't end up believing in anymore.

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:50.840
We have a down day, we
don't have that big boldness

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.806
or that motivation all the time.

00:13:52.806 --> 00:13:56.894
Structuring into your
daily routine, the why.

00:13:56.894 --> 00:13:59.235
Why's it's so important to
you, why you're going to hold

00:13:59.235 --> 00:14:01.867
yourself back, where you know
you're going to fall down.

00:14:01.867 --> 00:14:04.821
For me, especially, when
my schedule's thrown

00:14:04.821 --> 00:14:06.535
off, that's where I start to fall down.

00:14:06.535 --> 00:14:09.007
I'm a pretty scheduled
person and I have different

00:14:09.007 --> 00:14:11.473
things on different days and
it really, really, really

00:14:11.473 --> 00:14:14.025
works well for me, the
system, the schedule works

00:14:14.025 --> 00:14:16.404
amazingly well for me
but on days when there's

00:14:16.404 --> 00:14:18.528
interruptions, it's
hard for me to get back

00:14:18.528 --> 00:14:20.786
on the schedule for the rest of that day.

00:14:20.786 --> 00:14:23.246
The next day starts, new
schedule, great to go.

00:14:23.246 --> 00:14:26.248
But if I fall off in
the middle of one day,

00:14:26.248 --> 00:14:28.534
it's really hard for me to catch back up

00:14:28.534 --> 00:14:31.284
and so it's either, I design
my schedule so that I don't

00:14:31.284 --> 00:14:34.085
have interruptions which
I've done for the most part.

00:14:34.085 --> 00:14:36.793
But there's still going to
be those five to 10% of days

00:14:36.793 --> 00:14:39.259
where something random,
mysterious happens that

00:14:39.259 --> 00:14:40.635
you have to adjust and deal with.

00:14:40.635 --> 00:14:42.391
And the second way to do it,
that I've been working on

00:14:42.391 --> 00:14:45.101
is having a trigger to
get you back on schedule,

00:14:45.101 --> 00:14:47.813
having a trigger to get
you back into the zone

00:14:47.813 --> 00:14:50.565
of where you want to be
and so what I do is I start

00:14:50.565 --> 00:14:53.112
my day with saying a few lines to myself.

00:14:53.112 --> 00:14:55.738
I'll say this three times
and if I can't start my day

00:14:55.738 --> 00:14:57.826
with it because there's been
some kind of interruption,

00:14:57.826 --> 00:14:59.570
then as soon as I'm ready
to start working again,

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:01.786
as soon as I need that extra
little jolt, as soon as

00:15:01.786 --> 00:15:05.202
I need to remember my why
and the push and the drive,

00:15:05.202 --> 00:15:08.115
then I read it again, ya know
what, let me read it for you.

00:15:08.115 --> 00:15:09.913
I'm going to pull it
out, this is what I read.

00:15:09.913 --> 00:15:12.929
This is how I start my day
and if I fall off track,

00:15:12.929 --> 00:15:14.853
I get back to this, I
read this three times.

00:15:14.853 --> 00:15:18.027
Today I will push myself
to be my absolute best,

00:15:18.027 --> 00:15:20.953
to believe more, care more and try harder.

00:15:20.953 --> 00:15:23.873
I vow not to let
distractions, schedule changes

00:15:23.873 --> 00:15:27.000
or fear prevent me from being great.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.548
I will make every minute count

00:15:28.548 --> 00:15:30.508
because my time is running out.

00:15:30.508 --> 00:15:32.004
I have the ability to change the world

00:15:32.004 --> 00:15:35.088
and it's my responsibility to do so.

00:15:35.088 --> 00:15:39.255
If you want to increase your
will power, remember you why.

00:15:42.008 --> 00:15:43.344
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:43.344 --> 00:15:46.231
I made this video because
Abilash asked me to.

00:15:46.231 --> 00:15:47.815
So if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:15:47.815 --> 00:15:50.525
on the next edition of
Believe Life, leave it down

00:15:50.525 --> 00:15:52.405
in the comments below and
I'll see what I can do.

00:15:52.405 --> 00:15:54.439
I'd also love to know, what
did you take from this video?

00:15:54.439 --> 00:15:55.897
What did you learn the
most, what are you going

00:15:55.897 --> 00:15:59.017
to do in your life or
your business to increase

00:15:59.017 --> 00:16:01.522
your will power, did I miss
something here that you

00:16:01.522 --> 00:16:03.896
want to share, leave it
down in the comments below.

00:16:03.896 --> 00:16:05.606
I love to hear from you,
finally, I wanted to

00:16:05.606 --> 00:16:07.312
give a quick shout out to 2000 Books.

00:16:07.312 --> 00:16:09.190
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:12.620
Your One Word and posting
that awesome picture

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:15.286
of you outside with it,
I really hope you enjoy

00:16:15.286 --> 00:16:17.288
the beautiful weather,
as well as the book.

00:16:17.288 --> 00:16:18.914
Thank you so much for your support.

00:16:18.914 --> 00:16:20.249
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:16:20.249 --> 00:16:21.995
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:16:21.995 --> 00:16:25.579
to believe in yourself and
whatever Your One Word is.

00:16:25.579 --> 00:16:29.903
Much love, have an amazing
day and I'll see you soon.

00:16:29.903 --> 00:16:34.070
(whooshing)
(basketball bouncing)

00:16:35.109 --> 00:16:39.276
- I think it's your natural
responsibility to be great.

00:16:41.114 --> 00:16:45.162
And I think for you not
to do whatever it takes to

00:16:45.162 --> 00:16:47.916
learn how to run your
mind like a superstar

00:16:47.916 --> 00:16:50.901
and to make this your
absolute best year yet,

00:16:50.901 --> 00:16:53.986
I think for you not to
invest in becoming the person

00:16:53.986 --> 00:16:57.605
you know you're meant to
be, I think for you to play

00:16:57.605 --> 00:17:00.769
small with your life, for
you to go to work and coast,

00:17:00.769 --> 00:17:03.319
for you not to do things
that are difficult, for you

00:17:03.319 --> 00:17:07.779
not to lean into your
fear, for you not to read,

00:17:07.779 --> 00:17:10.707
for you not invest in
your learning, for you not

00:17:10.707 --> 00:17:13.422
to populate your life
with people who are better

00:17:13.422 --> 00:17:17.172
thinkers than you, is
being out of integrity.

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.924
And I think it's being
out of integrity to you,

00:17:21.924 --> 00:17:24.596
to your family and to the world.

00:17:24.596 --> 00:17:26.228
And really, and I know
mostly we don't talk about

00:17:26.228 --> 00:17:29.533
high performance and peak
potential in terms of

00:17:29.533 --> 00:17:33.951
integrity but you have a
personal obligation as do I,

00:17:33.951 --> 00:17:37.159
to be the best human being
and to express the gifts

00:17:37.159 --> 00:17:38.993
and the talents you were born with.

00:17:38.993 --> 00:17:40.743
And if you don't do that
because you've fallen into

00:17:40.743 --> 00:17:43.249
mediocrity or because you've
bought a bill of goods

00:17:43.249 --> 00:17:46.671
that the world has sold
you, that you're average,

00:17:46.671 --> 00:17:49.184
that you're average, that
you're ordinary, that the

00:17:49.184 --> 00:17:51.810
Beckham's and the Jay
Z's and the Mandella's

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:56.734
are somehow different from you,
well, that's just not true.

00:17:56.734 --> 00:18:00.152
And you are breaching your
own integrity and your own

00:18:00.152 --> 00:18:02.648
responsibility and if I do the same thing,

00:18:02.648 --> 00:18:05.615
I'm equally responsible
because the world is less of a

00:18:05.615 --> 00:18:08.117
place and your family is less happy

00:18:08.117 --> 00:18:11.499
because you're not living at your best.

00:18:11.499 --> 00:18:15.505
And related to that,
will power and expressing

00:18:15.505 --> 00:18:18.215
your potential and playing
a genius and creating

00:18:18.215 --> 00:18:22.476
a life that's legendary is
actually the secret to happiness.

00:18:22.476 --> 00:18:24.312
I went for a little
walk before the webinar

00:18:24.312 --> 00:18:28.479
and I thought to myself,
ya know, full expression of

00:18:29.736 --> 00:18:33.320
your will power is really
how you express your genius

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:36.030
and how you express the
genius you were born into.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:38.280
But it's also the secret to happiness.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:41.375
I mean, we watch Breaking
Bad or we drink too much

00:18:41.375 --> 00:18:43.877
or we gossip too much or
we spend too much time

00:18:43.877 --> 00:18:47.091
on the internet and we think
we're doing that to keep

00:18:47.091 --> 00:18:49.931
us happy and you've read my
books and you've followed

00:18:49.931 --> 00:18:52.055
me so you know I believe that victims

00:18:52.055 --> 00:18:55.017
love entertainment,
leaders love education.

00:18:55.017 --> 00:18:57.522
Ordinary people love
leisure and extraordinary

00:18:57.522 --> 00:18:59.730
people invest in their learning.

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:01.022
I mean, I looked at the best of the best.

00:19:01.022 --> 00:19:03.312
I look at the billionaires
that I've coached,

00:19:03.312 --> 00:19:07.479
NBA players who follow my work,
Taylor Swift reads my books.

00:19:08.688 --> 00:19:11.530
FC Barcelona reads The
Monk Who Sold His Ferrari.

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:14.552
John Bon Jovi read The
Monk Who Sold His Ferrari

00:19:14.552 --> 00:19:17.354
and I say that simply to share with you.

00:19:17.354 --> 00:19:19.812
If you look at the best of the best,

00:19:19.812 --> 00:19:22.818
they are the best of
the best in full passion

00:19:22.818 --> 00:19:27.287
in excellence and exuberance
because they stretch.

00:19:27.287 --> 00:19:29.961
Because they want to be the best
and let's go to the science.

00:19:29.961 --> 00:19:32.131
Every time you do something uncomfortable,

00:19:32.131 --> 00:19:35.801
every single time you exercise
self control and will power,

00:19:35.801 --> 00:19:39.007
you release a neuro
transmitter called dopamine.

00:19:39.007 --> 00:19:41.591
Dopamine is the secret to happiness.

00:19:41.591 --> 00:19:45.884
Dopamine is the neuro
transmitter of motivation.

00:19:45.884 --> 00:19:49.634
And it doesn't happen playing
Grand Theft Auto Live.

00:19:49.634 --> 00:19:52.510
It's doesn't happen gossiping
at the water cooler.

00:19:52.510 --> 00:19:56.048
It doesn't happen being
addicted to distraction.

00:19:56.048 --> 00:19:59.833
Dopamine is released when
you do difficult things,

00:19:59.833 --> 00:20:03.982
when you are focused, when
you achieve a small win

00:20:03.982 --> 00:20:06.232
and you say yeah, I did it.

